<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Dejanović</h1><p class="st-meta">1371 CE – 1395 CE · capital Velbazhd</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Lordship of the Dejanović brothers in eastern Macedonia and western Bulgaria, Ottoman vassals whose daughter became a Byzantine empress.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The sebastokrator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dejan-sebastokrator">Dejan</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> and brother-in-law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a>, held lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumanovo">Kumanovo</a> in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbian-empire">Serbian Empire</a>. After Dušan's death his sons <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jovan-dragas">Jovan Dragaš</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstantin-dragas">Konstantin Dragaš</a> built an autonomous lordship stretching from Kumanovo to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyustendil">Velbazhd</a> (Kyustendil) and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strumica">Strumica</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The brothers ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyustendil">Velbazhd</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strumica">Strumica</a>, taxing the trade routes between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vardar">Vardar</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/struma">Struma</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-maritsa">Maritsa</a> in 1371 they became Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>, supplying troops. They endowed monasteries on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/monastic-community-of-mount-athos">Mount Athos</a> and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-region">Macedonia</a>. Konstantin's daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helena-dragas">Helena</a> married the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-ii-palaiologos">Manuel II</a> and was the mother of the last emperor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-xi-palaiologos">Constantine XI</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Jovan died around 1378. Konstantin was killed fighting as an Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rovine">Rovine</a> in 1395, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> annexed his lands.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1371 CE – 1395 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:86.99%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1371 CE – 1395 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Velbazhd</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jovan Dragaš, Konstantin Dragaš</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Serbian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a>, <a href="/countries/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, <a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dejanović lands, Velbazhd lordship</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1383&amp;focus=lordship-of-dejanovic" aria-label="Lordship of Dejanović on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5201 700 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Dejanović lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5521 939h0M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5521 956h0"/><path class="map-do